filter-env oracle case: captured-phases-install-buildinfo

Isolates the real build-info save inside __dyn_install
(___save_and_filter_ebuild_env --exclude-init-phases --filter-path
--filter-sandbox --allow-extra-vars, the same option set as the
merge-time PORTAGE_UPDATE_ENV regen): the 2366-byte
--allow-extra-vars pattern, which filters PATH and SANDBOX_* but lets
the saved-readonly set (A/CATEGORY/PVR/PF/PN/PR/PV/P) through.
HOSTNAME stays filtered -- it also arrives via bash's own dynamic
variable list, which --allow-extra-vars does not cover. The pattern
additionally carries LD_PRELOAD plus SANDBOX_DENY/PREDICT/READ/
VERBOSE/WRITE as dynamic entries: this save runs sandboxed, and
libsandbox re-injects those variables even into the `env -i` probe
that collects bash's variables, so the "hygienic" list is not
hygienic here (verified: `sandbox env -i bash -c '... ${!L*} ...'`
still reports them).
If the native port regressed to the --filter-features shape here
(filtering the extra vars, or failing to filter PATH), out would
differ byte-for-byte.

Run exactly as the phase runtime runs it:
  /usr/bin/python <checkout>/bin/filter-bash-environment.py "$(cat args)" < in > out 2> stderr.txt
Byte-exact: the args file bytes are argv[1] (no trailing newline
added, none present); the in file bytes are stdin verbatim.

Provenance (D4):
  portage-ref: portage-3.0.82.2
  portage-commit: 1d95fc2c552a2c7d347e54093fa0e5b172a57004 (3rdparty/repos.toml [portage] commit)
  python: Python 3.14.8 (/usr/bin/python)
  capture: instrumented real Portage in bed container
    localhost/test-portuale:latest (Portage 3.0.82.2, container python 3.14.6)
    with bin/filter-bash-environment.py replaced by a logging
    wrapper (argv[1] + stdin recorded per call, then the real
    script re-executed with identical argv + stdin).
    ebuild | command | EBUILD_PHASE: porttest/porttest/phases/phases-1.0.ebuild | install | install
    EMERGE_FROM=ebuild (the ebuild(1) branch, same pattern
    branch as a source merge; the binary-merge branch and the
    preprocess --filter-locale/--filter-path/--filter-sandbox
    option set did not occur in these runs).
  sizes: args=2366 in=21904 out=11582
  date: 2026-10-08 (UTC day granularity; the only field that may change
    between regenerations)
